      "text": " <think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 32 and 56, we can use the standard multiplication method. This involves multiplying each digit of one number by each digit of the other number and then adding the results. Let's break it down step by step.\n...\n</think>\n<answer>\nFirst, let's write the numbers one above the other for clarity:\n```\n  32\n\u00d7 56\n```\nWe can break down the multiplication into two parts:\n1. Multiply 32 by 6 (the ones digit of 56).\n2. Multiply 32 by 50 (the tens digit of 56, which is 5 multiplied by 10).\n\nLet's start with the first part:\n```\n  32\n\u00d7  6\n```\nTo multiply 32 by 6, we can break it down further:\n- 30 \u00d7 6 = 180\n- 2 \u00d7 6 = 12\nAdding these together:\n180 + 12 = 192\nSo, 32 \u00d7 6 = 192.\n\nNow, let's move to the second part:\n```\n  32\n\u00d7 50\n```\nTo multiply 32 by 50, we can use the distributive property of multiplication over addition:\n- 32 \u00d7 50 = 32 \u00d7 (5 \u00d7 10) = (32 \u00d7 5) \u00d7 10\n- First, calculate 32 \u00d7 5 = 160\n- Then, multiply by 10: 160 \u00d7 10 = 1600\n\nNow, we add the results of the two parts together:\n192 (from 32 \u00d7 6) + 1600 (from 32 \u00d7 50) = 1792\n\nTherefore, the product of 32 and 56 is 1792.\n</answer>",
