      "text": " <think>\nTo solve the problem of finding the product of 81 and 36, we can follow these steps:\n1. First, let's consider the numbers 81 and 36. 81 is a multiple of 9 (9 x 9 = 81), and 36 is also a multiple of 9 (9 x 4 = 36).\n2. We can use the distributive property of multiplication over addition to make the calculation easier. We can break down 81 into 9 x 9 and 36 into 9 x 4.\n3. Now, we can rewrite the multiplication as: (9 x 9) x (9 x 4)\n4. According to the associative property of multiplication, we can rearrange the factors without changing the product. So, we can group the factors as: (9 x 9) x (4 x 9)\n5. Now, we can multiply the numbers inside the parentheses first: 9 x 9 = 81 and 4 x 9 = 36\n6. Finally, we multiply the results of the two multiplications: 81 x 36\n7. To make the multiplication easier, we can break down 36 into 4 x 9: 81 x (4 x 9)\n8. Now, we can use the associative property again to group the factors: (81 x 4) x 9\n9. Let's calculate 81 x 4: 81 x 4 = 324\n10. Now, we have 324 x 9. To make this multiplication easier, we can break down 9 into 10 - 1: 324 x (10 - 1)\n11. Using the distributive property, we can distribute the multiplication: 324 x 10 - 324 x 1\n12. Now, we can calculate each part separately: 324 x 10 = 3240 and 324 x 1 = 324\n13. Finally, we subtract the second result from the first: 3240 - 324 = 2916\n</think>\n<answer>\nThe product of 81 and 36 is 2916.\n</answer>",
